I assume you're talking about MR and reflection.
For fixing reflection (and this may well have been suggested before),
how about a system where each refelction-granting item only gives a
percentage of coverage. These could stack. For example, an amulet is
quite small, and the chances of the ray or beam or whatever actually
hitting it are low, so an amulet on its own would reflect, say, 5% of
all incoming reflectable attacks. dragon armour gives much greater
coverage, so that would give you an additional 70% protection. All
sources of reflection would stack together up to a maximum of 99%.
Of course this means that some beams/ rays/ whatever WILL get through,
so they may have to be made either more avoidable or offer protection
by other means or make them somewhat less instadeathy, but then I
guess that's the root of the problem already, so if you fix that you
don't need to fix the way reflection is implemented. I'll just shut
up, shall I?



